    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a6ea048_05f28d5e",
        "filename": "audio/effect/all-versions/vts/functional/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T17:43:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that due to \"vts-core\" it is possible to run these tests correctly in presubmit. Current issue with \"general-tests\" is that atest doesn\u0027t take into account \"binary-test-disable-framework\" and \"binary-test-stop-native-servers\" statements from the test xml config, and leaving framework and native servers running can interfere with VTS.",
      "parentUuid": "5d0c0ba7_965f1a23",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "9d6c5163baa63882b1f8345d8bbe8d6aa5843663",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba87c300_20892bcd",
        "filename": "audio/effect/all-versions/vts/functional/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T18:00:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "just to clarify, tests only need to be in general-tests or device-tests to be accessible by presubmit test run, e.g., through Test Mapping. Adding it to vts-core is for the test to be part of vts-core compliance suite (for OEM).\n\nThe missing \"binary-test-disable-framework\" option should be added to the test xml files in this CL.\nNote that it\u0027s a vts option. To be translated to TradeFed config:\n\"binary-test-disable-framework\" is equivalent to:\n\t\u003ctarget_preparer class\u003d\"com.android.tradefed.targetprep.RunCommandTargetPreparer\"\u003e\n\t\t\u003coption name\u003d\"run-command\" value\u003d\"stop\"/\u003e\n\t\t\u003coption name\u003d\"teardown-command\" value\u003d\"start\"/\u003e\n\t\u003c/target_preparer\u003e\n\n\"binary-test-stop-native-servers\" is only related to vts harness (\"vts.native_server.on\" system property). Since the test will be a generic native test that doesn\u0027t require vts harness, the option is no longer needed.",
      "parentUuid": "3a6ea048_05f28d5e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "9d6c5163baa63882b1f8345d8bbe8d6aa5843663",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ccc8133_588bf4cf",
        "filename": "audio/effect/all-versions/vts/functional/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T18:19:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Dan!\n\nAnd is an equivalent for \"binary-test-stop-native-servers\"? In practice, this results in issuing the following command: \"adb shell setprop vts.native_server.on 1\"\n\nNelson, could you please add these commands to the XML files? I know that effects tests usually pass even if you don\u0027t satisfy these conditions, but depending on the framework activity they might fail.",
      "parentUuid": "ba87c300_20892bcd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "9d6c5163baa63882b1f8345d8bbe8d6aa5843663",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12278a13_3cf1edfc",
        "filename": "audio/effect/all-versions/vts/functional/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T18:24:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When running the test as native test through TradeFed, we don\u0027t rely on VTS harness (native server) to do service discovery. So I don\u0027t think the option \"binary-test-stop-native-servers\" will be applicable any more. And there is no equivalent TradeFed option, as we won\u0027t install vts native server on the device.",
      "parentUuid": "3ccc8133_588bf4cf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "9d6c5163baa63882b1f8345d8bbe8d6aa5843663",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3305ab23_55a0d83a",
        "filename": "audio/effect/all-versions/vts/functional/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T18:30:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s clarify this. For audio VTS, toggling \"vts.native_server.on\" also means that native audio_server process exits. This is important because audio HAL only supports 1 client correctly, having 2 clients: audio_server and VTS test often leads to test failures (especially for the \"core\" audio HAL VTS). So we still need this option to run VTS tests properly. We can introduce another property specific to audio_server if you plan to retire VTS harness native server.",
      "parentUuid": "12278a13_3cf1edfc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "9d6c5163baa63882b1f8345d8bbe8d6aa5843663",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d6e739d_1d870fd8",
        "filename": "audio/effect/all-versions/vts/functional/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T18:59:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "based on the chat with Mikhail, the audio test relies on property \"vts.native_server.on\" to make sure audioserver is stopped during the test run. Therefore, we need to continue using the property even though the new test run through TF won\u0027t install vts native server. \nWe can update the target preparer as follows. That way, the test will also keep working with vts test harness.\n\n\t\u003ctarget_preparer class\u003d\"com.android.tradefed.targetprep.RunCommandTargetPreparer\"\u003e\n\t\t\u003coption name\u003d\"run-command\" value\u003d\"stop \u0026\u0026 setprop vts.native_server.on 1\"/\u003e\n\t\t\u003coption name\u003d\"teardown-command\" value\u003d\"start \u0026\u0026 setprop vts.native_server.on 0\"/\u003e\n\t\u003c/target_preparer\u003e",
      "parentUuid": "3305ab23_55a0d83a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "9d6c5163baa63882b1f8345d8bbe8d6aa5843663",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
